# Lecture 11F

## UPGMA Group Activity: Class Problem

## Chapter 11

## Dr. Neil Voss

## November 17, 2026

=== layout: bookend

# Learning Objectives

@body

- Build a gene tree from the worksheet distance matrix.
- Update cluster distances after each merge.
- Calculate node heights and branch lengths.
- Explain how the tree summarizes the distances.

=== layout: section

# Gene Tree Group Activity

=== layout: one-panel

# Work With Your Group

@body

- Use your existing six-gene worksheet and its distance matrix.
- Try each step on your worksheet before the answer appears.
- Compare your calculations and tree with your group.
- Explain any differences before moving to the next step.

=== layout: subsection

# Plan Your Steps

=== layout: one-panel

# At Each Step

@body

1. Find the smallest distance and join those clusters.
2. Calculate the new node height: distance / 2.
3. Update the matrix using the original gene-pair distances.
4. Draw branches: parent height - child height.
5. Repeat until all six genes are in one tree.

@speaker-notes

Pause for group discussion before showing each answer.

=== layout: one-panel

# Follow the Join Colors

@body

- [*Join 1*]{color=#D40000}
- [*Join 2*]{color=#6C6C00}
- [*Join 3*]{color=#00775F}
- [*Join 4*]{color=#0067CC}
- [*Join 5*]{color=#CC0066}

New branches use the current join color. Earlier branches keep their colors.


