# Check Your Tree

@left

- What is the fitted tree distance from a to c?
- What is the fitted tree distance from a to b?
- Why can the a-to-b answer differ from the worksheet value of 12?

@right

![Completed metric gene tree](assets/lect11_gene_tree_examples/six_5.svg)

=== layout: two-panels

# Check Your Tree: Answers

@left

- a to c: 2 + 2 = 4, matching the original distance.
- a to b: 2 + 3 + 2 + 3 = 10; the original distance is 12.
- The tree fits cluster averages; it does not preserve every original pairwise distance.

@right

![Completed metric gene tree](assets/lect11_gene_tree_examples/six_5.svg)


=== layout: bookend

# Key Takeaways

@body

- Join the closest clusters and update the matrix after each merge.
- Use half the join distance for the new node height.
- Subtract child height from parent height for each branch.
- Compare distances along tree paths with the original distances.

